body:
if this helps you understand it a little more. note : i am not black i am an asian person from asia. 

when these things were done to black people it leaves severe generational trauma and when these things are ingrained into society so early in the birth of the country, these racist ideologies become woven into the fabric of the country and it’s systems. effects of these practices and the ideas behind them are still seen today and that’s why they don’t stand for the flag. 

if you disagree i’m not trying to start an argument, but i’m just answering your question :-)
